{"occurrence_id": "eliot-middlemarch-815a46cf243f6caf", "work_id": "eliot-middlemarch", "language": "en", "canonical_sha256": "db33091e5dfb388041d13c5037409b0b08833628d3b06c24ab7fd9f522249923", "pattern_version": "0.10", "pattern_id": "en_present", "match": "I love you", "start": 1724692, "end": 1724702, "context_start": 1724621, "context_end": 1725038, "context": "“There is no hope for me,” said Will. “Even if you loved me as well as\nI love you—even if I were everything to you—I shall most likely always\nbe very poor: on a sober calculation, one can count on nothing but a\ncreeping lot. It is impossible for us ever to belong to each other. It\nis perhaps base of me to have asked for a word from you. I meant to go\naway into silence, but I have not been able to do what I meant.”", "candidate_status": "candidate", "extraction_tool_version": "1.0", "form_family": "present", "polarity": "affirmative", "tense_aspect": "present", "temporal_modifier": "optional", "syntactic_family": "main_or_embedded"}
